# Media naming guide

Managed by Ansible (`ansible/roles/jellyfin`) — edit the template in the repo, not this file.

## Where things go

```
{{ jellyfin_media_root }}/
├── incoming/     drop uploads here; Jellyfin cannot see this tree
└── library/      mounted read-only at /media inside the container
```

Upload into `incoming/<kind>/`, rename to the conventions below, then move it across:

```bash
mv "{{ jellyfin_media_root }}/incoming/films/Dune Part Two (2024)" \
   "{{ jellyfin_media_root }}/library/films/"
```

Both trees are on the same filesystem, so the move is atomic — Jellyfin never sees a
partially copied file. Copying straight into `library/` defeats the point.

## Libraries

| Folder under `library/` | Jellyfin content type | Path to enter in the UI |
|---|---|---|
{% for lib in jellyfin_libraries %}
| `{{ lib }}/` | {{ jellyfin_library_types[lib] }} | `/media/{{ lib }}` |
{% endfor %}

Anime is split because a library folder may only hold one content type.

## Naming

The year in parentheses is what makes metadata matching reliable. Use it on the folder
and on the file.

**Films, documentaries, anime films** — one folder per film:

```
films/Blade Runner 2049 (2017)/Blade Runner 2049 (2017).mkv
documentaries/Free Solo (2018)/Free Solo (2018).mkv
anime/films/Spirited Away (2001)/Spirited Away (2001).mkv
```

**Series and anime series** — one folder per show, one per season:

```
series/Severance (2022)/Season 01/Severance (2022) S01E01.mkv
anime/series/Frieren (2023)/Season 01/Frieren (2023) S01E01.mkv
```

Season folders are `Season 01`, `Season 02`, … (`Specials` for season 0). Episodes are
`SxxEyy`. A double episode is `S01E01-E02`.

**Music** — artist, then album with year:

```
music/Boards of Canada/Music Has the Right to Children (1998)/01 Wildlife Analysis.flac
```

**Audiobooks** — author, then book with year:

```
audiobooks/Andy Weir/Project Hail Mary (2021)/01 - Chapter 1.m4b
```

**Podcasts** — show, then episode with year. MeTube files them this way when the
*Podcast* preset is ticked:

```
podcasts/All-In Podcast/Episode Title (2026)/01 Episode Title.opus
```

**YouTube** — channel, then video with year. MeTube files every video download here:

```
youtube/Big Think/Video Title (2025)/01 Video Title.webm
```

## Extras

Several qualities of the same film live side by side in its folder:

```
films/Dune (2021)/Dune (2021) - [2160p].mkv
films/Dune (2021)/Dune (2021) - [1080p].mkv
```

Bonus material goes in an `extras/` subfolder, or uses a suffix Jellyfin recognises —
`-trailer`, `-behindthescenes`, `-deleted`, `-interview`:

```
films/Dune (2021)/Dune (2021)-trailer.mkv
```

External subtitles sit next to the video, tagged with a language code:

```
films/Dune (2021)/Dune (2021).en.srt
films/Dune (2021)/Dune (2021).de.forced.srt
```

## Gotchas

- `/media` is mounted **read-only**. Jellyfin writes all metadata and artwork into its
  own config volume, never next to your files.
- After moving files in, trigger *Dashboard → Scheduled Tasks → Scan All Libraries*
  rather than waiting for the periodic scan.
- Adding a new library is a one-line change to `jellyfin_libraries` in
  `ansible/roles/jellyfin/defaults/main.yml`, then re-run the role — do not mkdir by
  hand, the next run will not know about it.
